    },
    "body": "Thanks for your work on this! Editorially it looks great.\r\n\r\nI did an initial pass. I think this definitely needs review from multiple people given the size. I put my thoughts here as doing it line-by-line would probably be unwieldy.\r\n\r\n* Can download the hyperlink still be reconciled with the navigate algorithm? (Looks like yes.)\r\n* Nit: i.e. and e.g. trailing commas.\r\n* Why \"classic\" for \"classic history API state\" and not \"legacy\"?\r\n* Nit: I find the three letter variable names rather confusing. I would prefer sessionHistoryEntry or entry over she, for instance.\r\n* \"navigation API method tracker-derived result\" doesn't initialize _apiMethodTracker's_.\r\n* Missing word: \"that are not via navigation API methods\"\r\n* NavigationDestination isn't linked from IDL\r\n* The NavigateEvent's type attribute is never initialized. (This is a bit concerning as I guess it means the implementation wasn't written based on the specification.)\r\n* \"inner navigate event firing algorithm\" has a lot of magic around influencing the normal order of the event loop. Is this really unique to navigation or is there a deeper issue here?\r\n* \"user navigation involvement\" seems problematic in that isTrusted can be true for events dispatched by the user agent. Consider `onmessage = e => console.log(e.isTrusted);postMessage(\"x\")`. `click()` setting it to false seems more of an exception. Did not look at what `submit()` does here. It might be okay for a limited set of call sites, but then we ought to make that clear somehow. Perhaps by inlining it.\r\n* This doesn't impact BFCache, right?",
